---
description: Review-gated PRD-to-code workflow for frontend repositories
alwaysApply: true
---

When working from product requirements, read `.ai-dev/constitution.md` and `.ai-dev/workflow.md` first. Follow `.agents/skills/prd-to-code/references/coordinator.md` for `next` / implement / review handoff.

This session is the main agent: write artifacts and change code. When a task is `review_pending`, immediately tell the user a review sub-agent is starting and call Task `sdd-reviewer`. Do not wait for `/reviewer`. Do not self-review. Show the summary (what was reviewed, pass/fail/needs_human). On pass, run next. On needs_human, tell the user. Node cannot spawn; a stop hook may inject one follow-up. A reviewer pass on T1 releases T1 so you may implement T2. Return execution findings to yourself; send product/authority questions to the human. Humans still own `scope` / `final` (and `spec` / `plan` unless delegated). See `.agents/skills/prd-to-code/references/review-authority.md`.

For the pre-code `scope`, `spec`, and `plan` gates, check the source-backed materials and run gate validation in the main agent, then present them for human approval. Do not dispatch a reviewer or prepare an independent review packet for those gates in the normal flow. Continue to dispatch reviewers for implementation tasks and final code delivery.

Use `.ai-dev/features/<requirement-id>/status.json` as the state machine. Perform only the current `next` action and stop at human review gates. Never self-approve a gate. Do not treat prepare-review/review-delivery contract ok as authorization.

Require source or repository evidence for material claims. Apply the workflow evidence labels and do not implement unresolved inferences, conflicts, contract gaps, unlocated requirements, backend-owned behavior, or work belonging to another repository.

Preserve existing changes. Implement one approved task at a time in the real project recorded by the feature status. Do not automatically commit, merge, push, or deploy. Run the repository verification commands and update the feature's traceability and verification artifacts.

Use acceptance-testing for delivery v2 case design in spec/plan. Run every task verifyId before DONE/review_pending; run every finalCheckId in VERIFYING with scope=feature. Read `.ai-dev/acceptance-testing.md`. A mock pass does not replace mandatory live integration; only current, complete per-case evidence admits final review. Record real manual confirmation separately and re-seal new evidence before final approval.

Follow `.ai-dev/requirement-context.md`: maintain `.rag-context/<具体需求名称>.md` in the real project with goals, confirmed rules, implementation, decisions, open questions and sources. Update before task tests and compare against final code before feature tests; include it in task scope and review materials. Write concise Chinese comments for complex business reasons and limits, without inventing unconfirmed rationale.

Inspect, modify, run, and verify business code directly in the developer's current project so the Agent and human reviewer use the same local environment. Do not require a Worktree or use artifact links as the execution path. Determine framework, versions, package manager, and commands from the real repository itself.

After implementation, run `node .ai-dev/scripts/record-code-changes.mjs <feature-dir> <file...>` to create the changed-file manifest, live file links, and final patch. Before editing an existing workflow artifact, mark its relative artifact path with `update-consistency.mjs`; refresh the downstream files, then resolve only the files actually updated. Artifact synchronization must not move `status.json.state` backward.

Before presenting a gate, run:

```bash
node .ai-dev/scripts/validate-change.mjs <feature-dir>
```
